invariant: INV-60
file: ct.c
catches: test/ct-taint.sh
reason: ct_memeq returns at the first byte that differs, so its time
  tells how many leading bytes of two secrets agree. The loop's exit
  branches on a secret byte, and Memcheck reports the jump in every case
  that compares secrets: a tag check, ML-KEM's re-encryption and the
  signers' checks

--- old
    for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        diff |= (uint32_t)(a[i] ^ b[i]);
    }
--- new
    for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        diff |= (uint32_t)(a[i] ^ b[i]);
        if (diff != 0) {
            return 0;
        }
    }
